# OBSIDIAN DOCUMENTATION GUIDELINES

When writing documentation, notes, or creating diagrams for this project, assume the user will read them in Obsidian. You MUST format the output accordingly:

## 1. Markdown Documentation (*.md)
Read the rules in `.cursor/rules/obsidian-refs/obsidian-markdown.md`.
- Use `[[wikilinks]]` instead of standard markdown links when referencing other local documentation files.
- Use Obsidian Callouts (e.g., `> [!info]`, `> [!warning]`) for highlights.
- Include proper YAML frontmatter (Properties) for metadata.

## 2. Architecture & Diagrams (*.canvas)
Read the rules in `.cursor/rules/obsidian-refs/json-canvas.md`.
If the user asks for a visual architecture, flow chart, or diagram, generate a valid `.canvas` file following the JSON Canvas specification. Do NOT generate Mermaid.js unless specifically requested; prefer `.canvas` files.
